/* ============ URDU-SPEAKER TRAP TRAINER ============ */
var TRAPS=[
['embarazada = "embarrassed"','Estoy embarazada means "I am PREGNANT". For embarrassed say: estoy avergonzado/a.','Embarazada sun kar Urdu wala "sharminda" samajhta hai — lekin is ka matlab hai haamla (pregnant)!'],
['actual = "actual / real"','Actual means "current / present-day". For "actual/real" say: real or verdadero. El presidente actual = the current president.','"Actual" English jaisa lagta hai lekin Spanish mein is ka matlab hai "haal ka, maujooda".'],
['asistir = "to assist / help"','Asistir a... means "to ATTEND". For "to help" say: ayudar. Asisto a la clase = I attend the class.','Asistir = haazir hona (attend). Madad ke liye "ayudar" bolo.'],
['sensible = "sensible / wise"','Sensible means "sensitive" (emotional). For "sensible/wise" say: sensato.','Sensible = jazbati / hassas. "Samajhdaar" ke liye sensato.'],
['carpeta = "carpet"','Carpeta means "folder". Carpet is: alfombra.','Carpeta = file folder. Qaleen (carpet) ko alfombra kehte hain.'],
['éxito = "exit"','Éxito means "success". Exit is: salida.','Éxito = kamiyabi! Bahar nikalna (exit) = salida.'],
['librería = "library"','Librería is a BOOKSHOP. A library is: biblioteca.','Librería mein kitaabein BIKTI hain. Muft parhne ki jagah = biblioteca.'],
['recordar = "to record"','Recordar means "to remember". To record (audio/video) is: grabar.','Recordar = yaad karna. Record karna (recording) = grabar.'],
['sopa = "soap"','Sopa is SOUP (food). Soap is: jabón.','Sopa khane wali cheez hai (soup). Sabun = jabón.'],
['largo = "large / big"','Largo means "long" (length). Big/large is: grande.','Largo = lamba. Bara (big) = grande.'],
['b and v sound the same','In Spanish, B and V are pronounced almost the SAME (a soft "b"). "Vaca" sounds like "baca". Do not read v as English "v" with teeth on lip.','Urdu mein b aur v alag hain, lekin Spanish mein dono ek jaisi awaaz dete hain — naram "b".'],
['j sounds like English "j"','Spanish J is a strong throat sound (like Urdu خ): ojo = "okho", trabajar = "trabakhar". Never "j" as in "jam".','J = gala se "kh" ki sakht awaaz, Urdu ke خ jaisi.'],
['g before e / i','G before E or I is also the throat "kh": gente = "khente", girasol = "khirasol". Before A/O/U it is a normal hard g.','Ge / gi = "khe / khi". Ga / go / gu = aam g.'],
['h is pronounced','H is ALWAYS silent in Spanish: hola = "ola", hotel = "otel", habla = "abla".','H hamesha khamosh hota hai — parha hi nahi jata.'],
['el problema (not la)','Words ending in -ma from Greek are MASCULINE: el problema, el tema, el sistema, el idioma. Do not say "la problema".','-ma wale alfaz aksar "el" lete hain: el problema. Yeh Urdu walon ki aam ghalti hai.'],
['la mano (not el)','Mano (hand) is FEMININE: la mano, una mano — even though it ends in -o.','Mano -o par khatam hota hai lekin "la" leta hai. Yaad rakho: la mano.'],
['el agua (but feminine!)','Agua is feminine but takes "el" for sound: el agua fría (adjective still feminine — fría, not frío).','Agua ke saath "el" sirf awaaz ki wajah se aata hai; sifat (adjective) feminine hi rehti hai: agua fría.'],
['la gente = many "person"','Gente (people) is SINGULAR in Spanish: la gente es (not "son"). Use: las personas for plural subjects.','"Log" (gente) Spanish mein singular hai: la gente es amable.'],
['estar = for everything "to be"','Urdu has ONE "hona", Spanish has TWO: SER for identity/origin/job (soy de Pakistán) and ESTAR for states/places (estoy cansado, estoy en casa).','Urdu ka ek "hona" Spanish mein do hain — pehchan ke liye SER, haalat/jagah ke liye ESTAR.'],
['ser for clock time','Time uses SER: es la una, son las dos. Do not use estar for the clock.','Waqt (ghanta) SER se kehte hain: son las tres.'],
['gustar = "I like" as gustO','Never "yo gusto" for "I like". The thing pleases YOU: me gusta el té (tea pleases me).','"Gusto" bolna aam ghalti hai. Hamesha "me gusta" — cheez mujhe pasand aati hai.'],
['hambre is "hamburg" / food','Hambre (with h) means HUNGER: tengo hambre = I am hungry. It is feminine: mucha hambre.','Hambre = bhook! "Tengo hambre" roz ka jumla hai.'],
['double l (ll) is a letter sound','LL sounds like "y": me llamo = "me yamo", pollo = "poyo", llave = "yave". Never read it as double-L.','Ll = "y" ki awaaz. "Llamo" ko "yamo" parho.'],
['qu sounds like "k"','QU = "k" sound: qué = "ke", quiero = "kiero", queso = "keso". The u is silent.','Qu mein u khamosh hai: "quiero" = "kiero".'],
['ue after g: guitarra','In "guitarra" and "guerra" the u is silent too: "gitarra", "gerra". But in "pingüino" the ü IS pronounced "gwee".','Gue/gui mein u khamosh; ü (do nuqton wali) bolti hai: pingüino = "pingweeno".']
];

