var GRAM_UR=['Salam aur taaruf ka asaan tareeqa.','Ginti, qeemat aur umar.','Din, mahina aur waqt poochna.','Rang aur cheezein bayan karna.','Khandan ke log.','Khana order karna.','Pehchan ke liye SER, halat ke liye ESTAR.','Aam verbs ke maujooda zamane ke asool.','Sawaliya alfaz aur nishan ¿ ?.','Safar mein rasta aur jagah.','Kharidari aur paisay.','Rozana ke kaam wale verbs.','Guzra zamana: kal kya hua.','"Ja raha hoon" wala mustaqbil.','Sehat aur emergency jumlay.','Mobile aur internet alfaz.','Naukri ki baat-cheet.','Pasand aur raaye.','Dost ko bulana aur plan banana.','Poori guftagu ka review.','Mausam ki gap shap.','Doctor ko sahi alamat batana.','Ghar kiraya par lena.','Bank ka kaam Spanish mein.','Phone par sahi jumlay.','Mehman-nawazi aur tehwaar.','Shikayat naram lehje mein.','Apne gaon/sheher ki baat.','Khwab aur ummeedein.','Kahani sunane ke jor-toor.','"Ke liye" ke do roop: por/para.','Do guzray zamanay: kya hua vs kaisa tha.','Gustar ulta chalta hai: cheez pasand aati hai.','Apne aap par asar wale verbs (mirror words).','Raaye dena aur ittefaq karna.','WhatsApp, data aur calls gehrai mein.','Sarkari kaam aur formal Spanish.','Ghar ki kharabi theek karwana.','Pharmacy par theek dawai mangna.','Apni zindagi ki kahani.','Doosre ki khwahish ke liye subjunctive.','Narmee se "chahiye hota" — conditional.','Doosre ki baat aagay sunana.','Formal khat aur email ka dhang.','Akhbar ki zubaan samajhna.','Behes mein jeet, tameez ke saath.','Meeting aur call ki zubaan.','Tehwaar aur chhoti baatein.','"Agar…" wale jumlay.','Apni poori kahani — sab kuch mila kar.'];
var GRAM_MIST=['Do not say "estoy Farrakh" for your name — identity uses SOY.','Age is "tengo 23 años" (I HAVE years), never "soy 23 años".','Only 1 o’clock uses "es la una"; other hours use "son las…".','Azul and verde never change for feminine words: "camisa azul".','Hermanos means brothers AND sisters together.','It is "la cuenta" for the bill — "el menú" is only the menu.','Feelings NOW take ESTAR: "estoy cansado", not "soy cansado".','The yo form ends in -o: "yo hablo", never "yo hablas".','Spanish questions need BOTH marks: ¿ … ?','Ask the taxi price BEFORE sitting down: "¿Cuánto cuesta el viaje?"','"Me lo llevo" = I will take it — not "yo llevo" alone.','Reflexive mirror word goes BEFORE the verb: "me despierto".','Preterite -ar yo ends -é (hablé), not -o.','Voy a + infinitive: never conjugate the second verb ("voy a estudio" ✗).','"Me duele" + singular, "me duelen" + plural (los pies).','Wifi in Spanish is pronounced "wee-fee".','Jobs use SER without "un": "Soy maestro", not "soy un maestro".','Plural things: "me GUSTAN las frutas", not gusta.','"¿Quieres…?" needs the verb after it: "¿Quieres venir?"','Review lessons use Person B lines — say them aloud, not silently.','Weather uses HACER (hace sol), not ESTAR, for sun/heat/cold.','"Desde hace dos días" = for two days (still true now).','Rent is "al mes": "¿Cuánto es el alquiler al mes?"','"Sacar dinero" = withdraw; "ingresar" = pay in. Do not mix them.','Spain answers the phone with "¿Diga?", not "hola" alone.','"¡Felicidades!" works for birthdays AND weddings.','Start complaints softly: "Perdón, hay un problema…".','Use "hay" for "there is/are" in your village description.','Hopes: "Espero + infinitive" — "espero viajar", not "espero viajo".','Story glue order: primero → luego → de repente → al final.','POR = through/because; PARA = purpose/destination. When unsure about purpose, choose PARA.','Habits in the past = imperfect: "de niño, jugaba…".','The verb agrees with the THING liked: gusta (one) / gustan (many).','Mirror words: me, te, se — "se levanta" for él/ella.','"Tienes razón" — never "estás razón".','"Quedarse sin batería" = run out of battery.','At offices always use USTED, never tú.','"Está roto" (broken thing) vs "no funciona" (machine) — pick the right one.','"Me pica" = it itches; "me duele" = it hurts. Different!','A life story mixes past, present AND future — do not use one tense only.','After "quiero que" the verb MUST change: "que vengas", not "que vienes".','"Me gustaría" is polite; plain "quiero" can sound demanding to strangers.','Reported speech steps back one tense: dice → dijo, es → era.','Formal letters never start with "Hola" — use "Estimado/a".','Headlines drop el/la/un — do not copy that style in normal sentences.','Disagree with a softener first: "Entiendo tu punto, pero…".','"Quedamos en…" = we AGREED to… — not "we stayed".','"Llevar + time" = how long: "Llevo dos años aquí".','After "si" for real plans use the PRESENT, never the future.','Your final story: past for roots, present for now, future for dreams.'];

